Description: session launchers and units for fastrdp back ends
 fastrdp turns a Linux host into a multi-user RDP terminal server.
 .
 This package contains the session side:
  - startwm.sh for xrdp (starts the desktop chosen by the broker),
  - the headless Plasma (Wayland) launcher, its unit template and PAM stack,
  - the KWin virtual-backend drop-in for plasma-kwin_wayland.service,
  - the wlroots-in-x launcher, clipboard bridge and X session entries for
    Sway, labwc and Wayfire,
  - the xrdp-sesman PAM stack that accepts only broker tokens (installed
    as a template under /usr/share/fastrdp-session; copy it to
    /etc/pam.d/xrdp-sesman, the deployment roles do this),
  - tgt-notify, started in every desktop session (XDG autostart): a desktop
    notification before the session's Kerberos login can no longer be
    renewed (settings: /etc/fastrdp/tgt-notify.conf),
  - xrdp-audio, started in xrdp sessions (XDG autostart, wlroots-in-x): loads
    the PipeWire xrdp module of pipewire-module-xrdp, sink-only when the
    microphone is switched off.

